    "['access-list [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5] [parameter6]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 from source-address 192.168.0.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 from source-address 192.168.0.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 from source-address 192.168.0.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThe Juniper configuration:\\n1. Creates a firewall filter named ACL2000 (equivalent to Cisco\\'s ACL 2000)\\n2. Defines a term (term 1) that matches the source address 192.168.0.0/24 (equivalent to 192.168.0.0 with wildcard 0.0.0.255)\\n3. Uses \"then accept\" action which is equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"permit\"\\n4. The \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination match condition', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 from source-address 192.168.0.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 from source-address 192.168.0.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThe Juniper configuration:\\n1. Creates a firewall filter named ACL2000 (equivalent to Cisco\\'s ACL 2000)\\n2. Defines a term (term 1) that matches the source address 192.168.0.0/24 (equivalent to 192.168.0.0 with wildcard 0.0.0.255)\\n3. Uses \"then accept\" action which is equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"permit\"\\n4. The \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination match condition', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2000 term 1 then accept'}]]": 1,
    "['access-list [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5] [parameter6]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco access-list command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThis creates:\\n1. A firewall filter named ACL2001 (matching Cisco's ACL 2001)\\n2. A term 'term1' that matches:\\n   - Source address 192.168.1.0/24 (CIDR equivalent of 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255)\\n   - Any destination ('from' without destination specified implies 'any')\\n3. An accept action (equivalent to 'permit')\", 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco access-list command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThis creates:\\n1. A firewall filter named ACL2001 (matching Cisco's ACL 2001)\\n2. A term 'term1' that matches:\\n   - Source address 192.168.1.0/24 (CIDR equivalent of 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255)\\n   - Any destination ('from' without destination specified implies 'any')\\n3. An accept action (equivalent to 'permit')\", 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term term1 then accept'}]]": 1,
    "['access-list [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5] [parameter6]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. Juniper uses firewall filters instead of access lists\\n2. \"family inet\" specifies IPv4 processing\\n3. The filter is named ACL2001 to maintain similar numbering\\n4. A term is created for each permission entry\\n5. The source address uses CIDR notation (/24 equivalent to 0.0.0.255 wildcard)\\n6. \"then accept\" is equivalent to \"permit\" in Cisco', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. Juniper uses firewall filters instead of access lists\\n2. \"family inet\" specifies IPv4 processing\\n3. The filter is named ACL2001 to maintain similar numbering\\n4. A term is created for each permission entry\\n5. The source address uses CIDR notation (/24 equivalent to 0.0.0.255 wildcard)\\n6. \"then accept\" is equivalent to \"permit\" in Cisco', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept'}]]": 1,
