    "['match ip address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement 1 term 10 from route-filter 192.168.0.0/24 exact', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset policy-options policy-statement 1 term 10 from route-filter 192.168.0.0/24 exact\\n## \\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, route-maps are translated to policy-statements\\n- The \"match ip address\" in Cisco becomes \"from route-filter\" in Juniper\\n- The ACL 2000 in Cisco (permitting 192.168.0.0/24) is translated to a direct route-filter for that prefix\\n- The \"term 10\" corresponds to the sequence number \"10\" in the route-map\\n- The \"exact\" modifier ensures the same behavior as Cisco\\'s standard ACL matching', 'trans_template': 'set policy-options policy-statement 1 term 10 from route-filter 192.168.0.0/24 exact'}]]": 1,
    "['match ip address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'from {', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `match ip address 2001` command:\\n\\n##\\nfrom {\\n    prefix-list 2001;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nThis translation assumes that ACL 2001 from the Cisco configuration has been converted to a Juniper prefix list named \"2001\". The Juniper `from` statement is used in route-maps (policy-statements in Junos) to match conditions, similar to Cisco\\'s `match` command.', 'trans_template': 'from {'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'prefix-list 2001;', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `match ip address 2001` command:\\n\\n##\\nfrom {\\n    prefix-list 2001;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nThis translation assumes that ACL 2001 from the Cisco configuration has been converted to a Juniper prefix list named \"2001\". The Juniper `from` statement is used in route-maps (policy-statements in Junos) to match conditions, similar to Cisco\\'s `match` command.', 'trans_template': 'prefix-list 2001;'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': '}', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interfaces [parameter2]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `match ip address 2001` command:\\n\\n##\\nfrom {\\n    prefix-list 2001;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nThis translation assumes that ACL 2001 from the Cisco configuration has been converted to a Juniper prefix list named \"2001\". The Juniper `from` statement is used in route-maps (policy-statements in Junos) to match conditions, similar to Cisco\\'s `match` command.', 'trans_template': '}'}]]": 1,
